ejong","html_url":"https://github.com/Eelkedejong","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eelkedejong/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eelkedejong/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eelkedejong/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eelkedejong/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eelkedejong/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eelkedejong/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eelkedejong/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eelkedejong/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eelkedejong/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-23T09:49:40Z","updated_at":"2025-04-23T09:49:40Z","body":"I was able to get the workaround to work only partially.\n\nThe `onValueChange/onChange` events can be used to clear the error state, but I'm unsure how to clear the `data-invalid` attribute.\n\nHere's an example of clearing the errors with `onValueChange`: https://codesandbox.io/p/devbox/jovial-worker-7k3xt9\n\nI tried to use the `invalid` prop to modify the `data-invalid`,  but that didn’t seem to work.\n\nWhen a `Select` field has the `data-invalid` attribute, it doesn't prevent the form from submitting (which might be a bug on its own? Because it probably should?). However, if a `Radio` field has `data-invalid`, it does block the form from triggering the `onSubmit`.\n\nIs there a way to implement the workaround for the` Radio` field, or another method to clear the` data-invalid` attribute?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2823732934/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]]